1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:03,779
The current self-hosted quick start
describes a single Linux-server

2
00:00:03,779 --> 00:00:05,940
evaluation using Docker Compose.

3
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:09,720
Plan separate web, API,
and events hostnames.

4
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:13,000
Infrastructure operation is
a separate learning path from

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,420
department administration.

6
00:00:14,599 --> 00:00:19,040
Review the supported installer, generate
deployment-specific credentials, and

7
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:21,070
inspect the resulting configuration.

8
00:00:21,449 --> 00:00:26,709
Start the stack, review worker migration
progress, and verify all three endpoints.

9
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:30,209
Create the first account and
department after initialization.

10
00:00:30,509 --> 00:00:33,489
Department screens configure
operational behavior.

11
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:37,320
In this checkout, host
configuration uses public static

12
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:39,320
fields in configuration classes.

13
00:00:39,679 --> 00:00:43,259
The configuration processor
reads JSON keys or environment

14
00:00:43,259 --> 00:00:45,259
variables and assigns those fields.

15
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:50,900
Use the source and release documentation
to identify the exact host setting; avoid

16
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:53,260
applying a generic appsettings recipe.

17
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:56,729
Before updating, back up the
data and configuration and

18
00:00:56,729 --> 00:00:58,729
retain prior image references.

19
00:00:59,099 --> 00:01:03,059
A rollback can require restoring the
database as well as the application.

20
00:01:03,439 --> 00:01:08,380
Treat a running evaluation as the start
of operations preparation, with monitoring

21
00:01:08,410 --> 00:01:10,269
and a tested recovery procedure.

22
00:01:10,619 --> 00:01:14,050
Detailed infrastructure capture
needs the chosen deployment layout:

23
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:19,900
Linux Compose, Windows, Kubernetes
or k3s, or an Incident Command Kit.

24
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:24,839
Record the supported release and verify
installation, endpoint connectivity,

25
00:01:25,099 --> 00:01:27,410
backup, and recovery in that environment.

26
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,430
Use the linked official guides
for the matching layout.
